The full symbolic claim exposed two K-backend issues rather than a semantic failure: very large surface terms trigger a proof-front-end bug, while naming the exact AST avoids that bug but makes arithmetic normalization expensive. I’ve isolated both with small passing claims and am now reducing the proof burden by preserving the exact AST while sharing its repeated subexpression at the verification layer.
