#Top

codex
The symbolic proof now closes cleanly. The key fix was semantic, not cosmetic: Python evaluates binary operands left-to-right, so changing K’s evaluation attribute from nondeterministic strictness to sequential strictness both matches Python and removes exponentially many equivalent proof paths. The claim now contains the exact constructor tree from `solution.mpy` and proves it for symbolic `N >= 1`.
